DHQuant builds on 2DQuant, BasicSR, and SwinIR.

2DQuant: Low-bit Post-Training Quantization for Image Super-Resolution
Kai Liu, Haotong Qin, Yong Guo, Xin Yuan, Linghe Kong, Guihai Chen, Yulun Zhang.
NeurIPS 2024. https://github.com/Kai-Liu001/2DQuant
The PTQ framework, uniform fake quantization, DOBI search, and distillation
calibration are derived from this implementation.

BasicSR: Open Source Image and Video Super-Resolution Toolbox
https://github.com/XPixelGroup/BasicSR
The basicsr namespace is retained for the vendored training, data, and metric utilities.

SwinIR: Image Restoration Using Swin Transformer
https://github.com/JingyunLiang/SwinIR
The backbone remains named SwinIR; DHQuant is the post-training quantization method.

DAS uses the equivalent channel-rescaling rule from SmoothQuant, as acknowledged
in Section III-C of the manuscript. HCG uses minimum/maximum channel descriptors,
whose prior use in range-based grouping is acknowledged to RPTQ in Section III-D.

Changes in this distribution include DHQuant/DAS/HCG naming, release configuration,
portable entry points, checkpoint validation, and calibration-data collection.
The Apache License 2.0 text supplied with the local 2DQuant baseline is retained.
